card.statement:
Let\/ $\pen\in\{\T,\Aster\}$.

- [(a)]
Two ${}^{\pen}$unitary representations $\mathcal A$ and $\mathcal B$ of a quiver $Q$ are isometric if and only if

\begin{equation}
\tr {\widetilde {\mathcal A}}(\pi)=\tr\widetilde{\mathcal B}(\pi)
\end{equation}

for each oriented cycle $\pi$ in the quiver $\widetilde Q$.

- [(b)] It suffices to verify <<ref:mcv>> for all cycles $\pi$ of length at most

\begin{equation}
\varphi((r+2)(d_1+\dots+d_t)),
\end{equation}

in which $(d_1,\dots,d_t)$ is the dimension of the representations $\mathcal A$ and $\mathcal B$ $($see <<ref:e3y>>$)$, $\varphi (n)$ is any bound
for the sufficient word length in Specht's criterion $($for example, $\varphi (n)$ is $n^2$ or Pappacena's bound <<ref:vrv>>$)$, and $r$ is the minimal natural number such that

\begin{equation}
\frac{r(r+1)}2\ge\max\{m_{ij}\,|\, \text{$i$ and $j$ are vertices of $Q$}\},
\end{equation}

in which $m_{ij}$ is the number of arrows from $j$ to $i$ in $Q$.
